All right, all right. Solar Jetman, a little bit of a story here for you.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:19.000
The Golden Warship was once the most powerful spacecraft in Solar Jetman's galactic fleet.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:23.240
But that was before alien space pirates shipnapped.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:25.080
I love that. Shipnapped.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:26.680
That's like I've never heard that word before.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:29.060
It's immediately in my dictionary now.

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:32.340
They shipnapped the vessel on its very last mission.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:36.740
What are the odds? The warship now lies disassembled and hidden throughout the galaxy.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:38.200
Why did they take it apart?

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:45.120
This is like that thing in like Zelda where it's like, why is Ganon leaving the keys in various rooms, right?

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.780
Shouldn't he just hold on to all the keys?

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.320
I mean, I think these are different situations.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.040
Like I think like, you know, Ganon...

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:53.780
You think that the ship fell apart as they were like transporting it?

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:58.720
No, I think that they're trying to hide so they can never be created again.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:02.080
Whereas I think Ganon is just very forgetful.

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:06.300
Yeah, maybe like they don't want to destroy it in case they ever need it.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:11.920
But it's too dangerous to just leave fully built anywhere because it could be stolen back and then it's an enemy.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:16.620
So they gotta like, yeah, they gotta hide it throughout the galaxy where only they know where it is.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:25.840
Like if I lose my wallet, like I know that I should just start scattering all of my credit cards and like driver's license and dollars.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.440
Yeah, rather than canceling them or anything.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:30.660
Yeah. Just scatter them. Make sure that they can't all be found at once.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.060
Yeah, well the numbers.

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:36.460
Each digit from your credit card number should be scattered throughout the country.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:37.720
I think my point stands though.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:39.120
You lost the credit card.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:42.280
It's now the person who found it scattered the credit cards.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:43.820
You know what I'm saying? That's what happened.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:46.900
They're making it harder for you.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:51.420
They're like, you know? Which, okay, it's fine because now we get the idea of the game, right?

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:59.660
You're gonna go to these various alien worlds and you're gonna try to retrieve the pieces of the golden warship using Jetman's...

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:03.300
Jetman's spaceship, which is not the golden warship.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.900
It's just some regular old space pod.

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:14.380
The whole hook of the game though isn't just like fly around on these alien planets and you know, shoot enemies.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:15.240
It's not a shmup.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:20.740
Don't shoot up a bunch of enemies and try to like collect the piece and then bring it back to the mothership.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:35.920
The whole hook of the game is that this is a like physics and gravity 101 workshop on the NES where the whole thing movement is influenced by inertia and momentum and your thruster on your ship.

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:39.300
So please, Joe, thoughts on that?

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:46.700
I mean, definitely a pretty unique experience from what we've played so far.

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:57.060
It, I did boot this up thinking it was gonna be a shmup and it was pretty cool at first just to see the physics based movement.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:03.040
Like it really is about the, you know, every game has its own physics, but this feels like it's about the physics.

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:11.440
You have to think about the way the gravity reacts to your ship on the first planet, which is different than the second planet, which is different than the third planet, etc.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:18.220
So it is a, it is not like a game where you're like, Oh, I've played this kind of thing a million times and I just gotta get the hang.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.280
I just gotta like figure out what this one's hook is.

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:25.660
Like this is a totally different experience than like a lot of other space based ship games.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:35.780
Yeah. I think that the easiest way to describe this game would be like, uh, just an expanded version of asteroids.

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:38.260
Uh, and that's great.

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:55.700
Like I think of the very classic, very simple arcade games of, of your, that's probably my favorite in terms of just like the, the very basic, uh, structure and like the whole, the whole physics thing.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:59.200
Uh, so I, I had a lot of fun with this game.

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:06.240
I'm glad you brought up Asteroid, Sean, uh, cause I actually meant to do that before talking about the, you know, just kind of ground everybody.

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:07.480
So I think that's a good point.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:11.740
One thing that's unique though, is like asteroids took place in space.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:17.120
So your ship, once you like gave a boost, right, it just kind of traveled in that direction.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:21.580
And if you reach the end of the screen, it just kind of looped back to the other, uh, end of the screen.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:25.440
And that's cool. Cause it wasn't like a, it wasn't just a straight line.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:31.360
It was like, if you were going diagonal, you would wind up in the corresponding diagonal end of the other, uh, part of the screen.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:40.160
But for solar jet man, since you're exploring like this alien world, it's always like bringing you back down to the ground.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:46.940
And so you do kind of have this more like constant need to thrust, uh, you know, gently too.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:53.100
You can't just give all your, you know, you can't just like send to a hundred cause then you're going to go flying in the other direction.

00:08:53.100 --> 00:09:04.020
You're always kind of like in need of pushing yourself, uh, both with and against where you want to go because you're not exploring in open sky.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:15.060
You're exploring, uh, like a cavern, a series of caves to try to find various items on, uh, these planets and the planets don't have the same, uh, gravity.

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:18.900
So it's not like, Oh, I'm, I'm going to, you know, like use the first level to like learn it.

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:22.300
It's like the next one might have looser or tougher physics.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:32.940
So I think all these things, uh, really spice up the gameplay, even if you already, uh, like, you know, got the gameplay loop on the first level.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:52.220
Yeah. It's not entirely like gravity from whatever planet you're on doesn't really play that much of a, of a factor here, which you might think, but definitely your ship is, is not as agile as like, you know, the little triangle from asteroids.

00:09:52.220 --> 00:10:00.240
And that actually might be like whenever your ship blows up, which we'll get to, um, how you control your guy.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:09.540
That might be a better analog for that, but it's not like just like trying to navigate these things with sort of like a heavy ship.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:16.280
Like you also are picking up objects that like via some kind of tractor beam, which are heavy as well.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:26.140
And not only are you then sort of fighting with that added weight, but you're also like trying to wrangle with the tension of the tractor beam.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:30.120
And if it's heavy enough, it may just start like pulling you.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:37.680
And so it, it's fun trying to, uh, figure out like these, like it's a problem solving.

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:43.860
It's, it's a much more methodical asteroids in that where it's kind of just like, how the hell do I get out of here with this thing?

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:48.060
Yeah. And those things that you're towing as you pick it up, you know, like you said, they're different weights and everything.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:49.040
They're also swinging.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:52.840
Yeah. And I was pretty impressed at like how, I mean, I don't know, I don't know how accurate it is.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.720
It feels accurate to me, but what do I know?

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:57.400
But like, it, it feels like it makes a huge difference.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:11:06.080
Like when it's swinging in one direction, you got to like really correct and, and think about your speed when, you know, you're going to try and stop abruptly or change directions.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:09.020
And then the thing is going to swing in the other direction and pull you away.

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:11.820
And it, it, it makes, it makes a big difference.

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:20.280
And I would really love to see someone who is like the number one in the world at solar jet man, just like speed run this game, because I'm sure it looks really cool.

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:23.160
But I feel like for most people playing this game, it's all about caution.

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:29.660
Yeah. Caution is a great point, Joe, because I think you try and, you try and go fast at first, right?

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:33.320
The thruster is, uh, it does allow you to go pretty fast.

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:40.100
So you do have to be careful once you enter the caves of like not, uh, hitting it too much or not throttling too much.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:49.840
But when you, with the swinging of whatever you're picking up, I didn't realize at first, like that the swinging, it almost makes it like impossible to move for a little bit.

00:11:49.840 --> 00:12:01.000
You know, it's, you have to wait for it to kind of become a straight line again, and then kind of force it in the direction you want to not, not moving around like too much, because then you'll start causing it to swing again.

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:12.540
And I, that extra piece of the momentum is essential to the challenge of the game because it's not enough to leave the mothership, go into the cave, find an item.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:30.320
Um, but then to bring it back to the mothership via this, um, you know, this rope system where you're kind of just taking it as cargo, that becomes like a whole new way of having to fight off enemies, get out of this cave, uh, not take too much damage.

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:36.760
Because your ship has, uh, you know, a certain amount of damage it can take, but it also has like a certain amount of fuel too.

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:54.400
Yeah, I, I really, and not only are you sort of wrangling with all these things that we've been describing, but they're like, once you get off that first rock, uh, you've also got these sort of spheres that may be in a tractor or a repulsor.

00:12:55.220 --> 00:12:57.600
And you have to, you have to deal with those.

00:12:57.740 --> 00:12:59.760
And at first I'm like, oh, I'm just screwed.

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:03.780
Like I ran into one of these things and I can't even get away.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:09.340
And even I'm like trying to like wiggle back and forth and trying to get some momentum that way.

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:15.660
And then I realized that like, oh, these things that you're picking up, like they're also sort of a progression system.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:29.380
And like, as you're picking up parts of the ship or just, or just objects of, of use, um, you'll get like a, like a force field or you'll get,

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:32.940
like a super boost, which is kind of necessary.

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:35.540
And I really liked the way that that works.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:41.140
Like it's kind of, it's not so much binary of is my thruster on or off.

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:45.900
Like you can also, uh, have, have a lot more thrust.

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:50.980
Uh, and, and now it's even more like of a dance that you're trying to do.

00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:55.960
So I really liked that whole progression with each object that you pick up.

00:13:56.600 --> 00:14:04.560
Yeah. I first, like, I, I kind of had the idea that like, oh, you're, I'll be able to upgrade my ship, but I wasn't really paying too much attention to it until I got to the second planet.

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:11.860
I think it wasn't, there's actually an item that's too heavy for me or, or whether it's too heavy or if it's like somehow magnetizing itself to the ground.

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:18.040
Uh, either way I needed to upgrade that thruster in order, in order to, to get to it.

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:23.560
And I thought that that was like, it does really feel like you're on an alien world exploring for parts.

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:30.980
You know, it's like that. It's like, you feel like you're a scavenger on another planet and you're as, whenever you go away from your base, you're in danger.

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:32.320
You have to manage your fuel.

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:34.840
You have to find parts to prepare your ship.

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:48.040
And I don't know, it does, it does give you that sort of like that idea that like that, maybe that thing that we've all like played make believe as a kid of like a space ranger or something like, you know, lost on an alien planet.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:50.060
We all did that, right? Absolutely.

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:54.900
Sure we did. You know, there's also a lot of optional stuff on each planet too.

00:14:54.900 --> 00:15:07.780
The only things you need to move on to the next planet is the piece of the golden space, a golden warship and, uh, the proper amount of fuel for the mother ship to, uh, be able to transport itself to the next planet.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:24.640
Everything else is optional, but there's good stuff on there because you, you know, uh, whether it's like diamonds or whatever, like there's things that you can basically accumulate enough points to then in between, uh, purchase additional weapons or, uh, equipment.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:32.560
From the, um, I think it's in the manual, it's referred to as the interstellar marketing company trading post, which is cool.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:36.340
Uh, but you, you can do that stuff as well, but it's all optional.

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:41.020
So it kind of becomes this, uh, you know, like how, how long do you want to stay on the planet?

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:46.080
It's up to you. And also how like risky do you want to be?

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:53.040
Because I think as Sean alluded to, if your, uh, ship does run out, uh, it's not game over.

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:58.320
Uh, you guys can tell me right now, but like, I actually thought it was going to be game over when, when the ship blew up.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:12.300
It was, it was a nice surprise to find out that solar jet man can then like, I guess via, uh, uh, jets in his own space, uh, suit can like continue to try to get back to the mother ship.

